/* ==================== Script 85 id="amiyo-step13-layer-transitions" ==================== */
/* ===== Export round 4, step 13: transitions on overlay / PiP tracks =====
   Found while testing multi-layer edits:
   1) Two clips of one overlay track overlap during a transition. The multi-layer painter took the OUTGOING clip, so the incoming clip (and its transition) never showed:
      the picture stayed on the old clip and then jumped. Fixed in activeVideoStack (incoming clip wins, like the single-track path).
   2) The outgoing picture of a transition was a copy of the WHOLE frame (base video, text, other layers), so a moving base video froze and ghosted while the transition ran.
      Now the outgoing clip is saved as its own transparent layer and only that layer is blended out.
   3) The multi-layer painter ignored the frame-accurate seek setting the export uses, so PiP pictures could be 2-3 frames old in an export. It now uses the same setting.            */
